k [unicode-bidi:inherit] [text-align:-webkit-match-parent] [text-align:match-parent]" data-code-line-group=""><span>   <span style="color: rgb(112, 184, 255);">git</span> <span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">add</span> <span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">README.md</span> <span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">screenshot.png</span>
</span><span>   <span style="color: rgb(112, 184, 255);">git</span> <span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">commit</span> <span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">-m</span> <span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">"Add README"</span>
</span><span>   <span style="color: rgb(112, 184, 255);">git</span> <span style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">push</span></span></span></code></pre></div></div></div>
<ol dir="ltr" start="4">
<li>Open your GitHub repo page. The README displays automatically below your files.</li>
</ol>
<p dir="ltr" data-cds-heading=""><strong>Two things to check</strong></p>
<ol dir="ltr">
<li><strong>Author name:</strong> you wrote “Zeeshan Ahmad” in one place and “Ishan Ahmed” in another. I used <strong>Zeeshan Ahmad</strong>. If that’s wrong, find the line <code dir="ltr">**Zeeshan Ahmad**</code> near the bottom of the README and change it.</li>
<li><strong>Your Model dropdown has a problem:</strong> the screenshot shows <code dir="ltr">gemini-nano-banana-2.1</code> selected by default. That is an <strong>image-generation</strong> model, not a chat model, so chatting with it will fail. Fix it in <code dir="ltr">app.py</code> by finding the <code dir="ltr">SKIP = (...)</code> list and adding <code dir="ltr">"banana"</code> to it, like this:</li>
</ol>
